# PyInstaller freeze environment (ws5 smoke test)
.venv-freeze/

# Session handoff notes, restart prompts and unsent outreach drafts. The
# `.local.md` suffix is the marker and it has always meant "not for the
# repo" — nothing matching it has ever been tracked. Ignored rather than
# merely conventional because a wide `git add` sweeps in whatever is
# untracked, and several of these are drafts addressed to real people.
#
# NOTE this is deliberately narrow. `scratch/` is NOT ignored: it is a
# tracked evidence directory (capture corpora, oracle runs), and hiding it
# would hide study output that belongs in the repo.
*.local.md

# NEC-5 Sommerfeld interpolation caches. A .NEX is a grid keyed to the
# medium and frequency, regenerated by the engine on demand — an
# intermediate, not an answer. The evidence a capture exists to preserve is
# the deck and the printout beside it. Matches what the tracked
# scratch/eznec-capture corpus already does (244 .NEC + 241 .OUT, zero
# .NEX); left implicit there, stated here because scratch/524-phase0 brings
# 33 MB of them and a wide `git add` would otherwise bank the lot.
*.NEX

# Probe block caches. A .npz here is a matrix block re-dumped so a probe can
# resume in seconds instead of minutes — scratch/524-phase2/PLAN.md calls
# them "cached" at every mention and names the regeneration cost (4 min for
# the fan tables). Same rule as the .NEX above: an intermediate, not an
# answer, and the answer is the JSON receipt beside it. 1.2 MB in
# scratch/524-phase2 alone, cited by nothing in either repo.
scratch/**/*.npz

# Licensed NEC-5 printouts inside the phase-2/phase-3 capture trees. A .OUT
# here is DERIVED: the deck beside it plus the licensed engine regenerates it
# exactly, so storing it banks another vendor's engine output in a PUBLIC repo
# to save a re-run. momwire#553's standing rule already says the licensed
# engine enters as a data oracle and that public artifacts carry conclusions,
# not its tables. The deck is the evidence and it stays.
scratch/**/probe*-nec5-cap/*.out
scratch/**/r5-captures/*.out
# Licensed NEC-5 printouts inside capture trees. A .OUT here is DERIVED: the
# deck beside it plus the licensed engine regenerates it exactly, so storing
# it banks 12 MB of somebody else's engine output in a PUBLIC repo to save a
# re-run. #553's standing rule already says the licensed engine enters as a
# data oracle and that public artifacts carry conclusions, not its tables.
# The deck is the evidence and it stays.
#
# index.json still NAMES the printout each capture produced — that is a
# record of what EZNEC wrote, not a promise the file is here; see the README
# in scratch/eznec-capture/.
#
# nec2c/4nec2 output is deliberately NOT covered: nec2c is open source, so
# its printouts are ours to publish and scratch/4nec2-capture keeps them.
scratch/eznec-capture/**/*.OUT
